{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Cartel Charter War","logline":"When cartographer Veya's new charts show the skybridges failing, the Bridge Wardens challenge the Drift Cartel's charter, and the toll-master Kael moves to bury the truth and seize the last stable routes while every isle is forced to choose a side.","theme":"Control costs more than it gains; truth is safer shared than hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Cracks in the Charter","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts","title":"The Fading Bridges","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to finish charting a safe route through the breaking skybridge network and confirm her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","conflict":"Her wind-sight shows several bridges shifting faster than any chart predicts, and her stubbornness makes her refuse to share unfinished findings with the Academy.","outcome":"She confirms the isles are drifting apart and that only a few stable routes remain, and she decides to take her charts to the Bridge Wardens at Emberroost.","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya reads the colours of the wind and finds proof that her mentor was right: the skybridge network is failing and the stable routes are running out."},{"id":"scn_emberroost_warning","title":"Cables at Emberroost","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants the Bridge Wardens to reinforce the failing routes using her charts.","conflict":"The Wardens report that forge-island supplies have been mysteriously short, and they blame the Cartel's sabotage and rising tolls. They cannot braid new cable without cloudstone.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to challenge the Drift Cartel's charter publicly, using Veya's charts as evidence. Veya reluctantly accepts the role and the risk.","summary":"At the forge-island, the Wardens see Veya's charts and link the failing bridges to the supply shortage and the Cartel's tolls, deciding to contest the charter.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_charts"]},{"id":"scn_docks_toll_master","title":"Kael's Ledger","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to secure the Cartel's monopoly on the last stable skybridge routes before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"Word of the Wardens' challenge reaches the docks. Kael admires Veya's skill but sees that her charts would expose how much of the network the Cartel is exploiting.","outcome":"Kael resolves to suppress Veya's charts, first by offering her a deal and, failing that, by pressuring those who shelter her.","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael learns of the Wardens' challenge, uses his ledger-mastery to find its weak points, and plots to bury the charts.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_warning"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Choosing Sides","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_offer","title":"The Rival's Offer","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to register her charts with the harbour authority. Kael wants to buy them and control them.","conflict":"The two former apprentices clash. Kael offers her recognition and wealth, which tests her fear of becoming like the ambitious Cartel leaders, and she refuses to let him control the charts.","outcome":"Veya rejects the offer and leaves, but the Cartel now knows exactly what she holds. Kael orders enforcers to watch her.","summary":"Kael offers to buy Veya's charts at Mistral Docks. She refuses, and the rivalry becomes open conflict.","depends_on":["scn_docks_toll_master"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_levy","title":"Grain and Levies","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed despite the Cartel levy.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers are closing in on her routes, and the Hollow Circle is split over whether to resist the levy or comply.","outcome":"Maris narrowly keeps one smuggling route open, and the Hollow Circle delays its decision about which side to take.","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris runs a grain shipment through the service corridors while enforcers tighten their grip.","depends_on":["scn_docks_toll_master"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_alliance","title":"Wind for Paths","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a hidden place to protect her charts and a way to bring the isles to the Wardens' side. Maris wants to protect her isle.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya will draw Cartel attention onto The Hollow, while Veya's stubbornness makes her dismiss Maris's caution.","outcome":"They trade wind-current knowledge for Maris's secret paths and form an uneasy alliance. Maris takes the risk of hiding Veya's charts in a silo.","summary":"Veya reaches The Hollow and bargains with Maris, forming an alliance that gives her cover and gives Maris safer routes.","depends_on":["scn_docks_offer","scn_hollow_levy"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_sabotage","title":"The Severed Cable","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to prove the Cartel is sabotaging the forges. Kael wants to discredit the Wardens before the charter hearing.","conflict":"A cable fails near the forge-pits in a way that suggests a spark in violation of the no-open-flame rule. Each side blames the other, and Kael uses the accident to say the Wardens are unfit to keep the bridges.","outcome":"The accident turns several isles against the Wardens, and Veya's own certainty leads her to accuse Kael without proof, which costs her credibility.","summary":"At Emberroost, a cable breaks and both sides trade blame. Kael turns the incident to his advantage and Veya's rash accusation backfires.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_alliance"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_betrayal","title":"A Flaw Exposed","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to re-verify her charts and rebuild trust. Maris wants reassurance that Veya will not endanger The Hollow.","conflict":"Veya's refusal to admit she misjudged the bridge failure at Emberroost puts her at odds with Maris, who must choose between loyalty to home and her friendship with Veya.","outcome":"Veya admits her error, re-checks her charts, and finds the one stable route that is also the key to the Cartel's monopoly. Maris stays, though still wary.","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya's flaw strains her friendship with Maris until she admits she was wrong, and the corrected charts reveal what is really at stake.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_sabotage"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Charter Hearing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_hearing","title":"The Charter Challenged","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to expose the failing network and the Cartel's hold on the last stable routes before the isles. Kael wants to defend the charter.","conflict":"Kael uses his ledger-mastery against the Wardens' case, while Veya must share her charts openly, giving up the hoarded control she had been protecting. Maris must show herself and her smuggling routes to prove the levy's harm.","outcome":"Veya shares her charts with every isle and Maris testifies, forcing the isles to choose, and a majority vote to void the charter's exclusive claim on the stable routes.","summary":"At the Mistral Docks hearing, Veya and Maris lay out the truth and force every isle to choose a side, while Kael fights to keep the charter intact.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_betrayal"]},{"id":"scn_docks_confrontation","title":"Price and Worth","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the last stable routes by force after losing the vote. Veya wants to stop him without becoming a hoarder of the routes herself.","conflict":"Kael threatens to cut the routes rather than share them, and Veya must resist the temptation to take control herself while his ledger-mastery picks at her weaknesses.","outcome":"Veya's open charts make his seizure pointless, and Kael realises that control costs more than it gains. He stands down.","summary":"Kael and Veya face off at the docks. Her openness defeats his control, and he is forced to concede.","depends_on":["scn_docks_hearing"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Charter","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_rebuild","title":"Braiding Anew","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"The Wardens want to rebuild the failing bridges. Kael must pay for the damage his supply sabotage caused.","conflict":"Wardens distrust Kael and Kael struggles to give up his belief that price equals worth, while the wind-debt rule means every crossing still has to be repaid.","outcome":"Kael supplies cloudstone to the forge-island under Warden oversight as repayment, and the first reinforced bridges are braided from Veya's charts.","summary":"At Emberroost, Kael atones by supplying cloudstone and the Wardens begin repairing the network using Veya's shared charts.","depends_on":["scn_docks_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"The Quiet Harvest","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants The Hollow's grain to flow without the levy. Veya wants to thank her and keep their friendship.","conflict":"Maris still trusts slowly and must decide whether Veya is a friend or a risk now that the crisis is over.","outcome":"The levy is lifted, Maris accepts Veya as a friend, and she recognises that hiding was a form of bravery.","summary":"In The Hollow, the grain moves freely again and Maris and Veya reaffirm their friendship.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_rebuild"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_new_charts","title":"Charts for Every Isle","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to record her mentor's theory and open the charts to all isles. Kael and Maris come to witness it.","conflict":"The isles are still drifting apart and the work is unfinished, so Veya must accept that recognition matters less than the shared work.","outcome":"The Academy publishes the open charts, crediting her mentor, and the three begin working on routes that stay safe for all.","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes the open charts in her mentor's name, with former rivals watching, and the isles face the drift together.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
</Output>
