for Maris's paths, forming an uneasy alliance that begins to fill in the chart.","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow, and Maris tests her before sharing the corridors; the exchange of wind lore for hidden paths seals their alliance.","depends_on":["scn_levy_at_the_mill","scn_cartel_demand"]},{"id":"scn_forge_sabotage","title":"Cables of Emberroost","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to check the braided cables at the forge-island to confirm which skybridges can still hold.","conflict":"The Bridge Wardens are short of supplies and suspicious of outsiders, and the rule against open flame means the two cannot examine the forge-pits without help.","outcome":"They find proof that cloudstone supplies were tampered with, which supports the Wardens' accusation against the Cartel and confirms that the stable routes are fewer than they feared.","summary":"At Emberroost, working within the no-flame rule, Veya and Maris examine the cables and discover tampered supplies that point to Kael's sabotage.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_close_in","title":"The Net Tightens","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to deliver grain through the docks to The Hollow's customers, and Kael wants to catch her and learn her routes.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery spots the weak point in her smuggling arrangement, and Maris must choose between running and protecting her friend's charts.","outcome":"Maris escapes but loses a shipment and a route, and Kael learns that Veya and Maris are working together.","summary":"At the docks, Kael corners Maris's shipment; she barely escapes, and Kael realises the charts and the grain are connected.","depends_on":["scn_forge_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_wind_debt_called","title":"Wind-Debt Called","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to finish the chart before the season's wind-debt is called, and Kael wants to use the debt to force her to hand it over.","conflict":"The wind-debt rule lets Kael demand repayment in goods or labour, and Veya's pride keeps her from admitting that her chart still has a gap she cannot close alone.","outcome":"Veya refuses to pay in charts and sees that her pride is endangering all of them, and Kael privately realises he cannot let her fail even as he cannot let her succeed.","summary":"Kael calls in Veya's wind-debt at Silverspine; the confrontation exposes Veya's flaw and Kael's inner conflict.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_veya_admits","title":"The Wrong Reading","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to repair her chart and her trust with Maris after discovering that one of her own readings was wrong.","conflict":"Veya must admit her error, and Maris, who rarely forgives, must decide whether to keep trusting a friend whose mistake cost her a shipment.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake aloud for the first time, Maris forgives her, and together they finish the chart, which needs Kael's ledger to show which routes can bear trade.","summary":"At The Hollow, Veya admits her wrong reading, Maris forgives her, and the two realise the map and the grain need the ledger to complete the plan.","depends_on":["scn_wind_debt_called"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Single Spell","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_offer_to_kael","title":"An Offer Across the Ledger","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want Kael to share his ledger so the chart can become a working plan, and Kael wants the charts to secure the monopoly.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and sees the offer as a trap, while Veya must give up hoarding her truth and Maris must trust an enemy.","outcome":"Kael sees that the three pieces form a single plan that none can complete alone, and he weighs the cost of control against shared survival.","summary":"The three meet at the docks, and Veya lays the chart, the grain and the ledger side by side so Kael can see they form one plan.","depends_on":["scn_veya_admits"]},{"id":"scn_weaving_the_route","title":"Weaving the Route","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"The three want to join the map, the grain routes and the ledger to reinforce the last stable skybridge before it collapses.","conflict":"The Bridge Wardens distrust Kael, the cartel loyalists oppose him, and every step must respect the no-flame rule while the bridge is failing.","outcome":"The combined route holds the last stable skybridge, and Kael gives up his claim to exclusive control, which costs him the monopoly.","summary":"At Emberroost, the chart, the grain and the ledger combine to hold the skybridge; Kael chooses shared use over control.","depends_on":["scn_offer_to_kael"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Weave Holds","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_levy_lifted","title":"The Levy Lifted","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants the grain levy ended, and Kael must decide whether to honour the new agreement.","conflict":"The Cartel loyalists and The Hollow Circle both doubt the agreement, and Maris has to forgive Kael without trusting him blindly.","outcome":"Kael lifts the levy and Maris opens the granaries on shared terms, easing the grain conflict.","summary":"At The Hollow, Kael ends the levy and Maris begins to share the grain openly instead of hiding it.","depends_on":["scn_weaving_the_route"]},{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Charts Shared","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the new chart so every isle can use it, and Maris wants to see her paths protected.","conflict":"Veya's old wish for recognition pulls against her decision to share, and the Cartel's former allies still want the charts withheld.","outcome":"Veya shares the charts with the whole archipelago and credits her mentor, Maris and Kael, which completes her change from hoarding truth to sharing it.","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes the new charts for all and credits her partners, showing that she has learned to share truth.","depends_on":["scn_levy_lifted"]},{"id":"scn_new_ledger","title":"A New Ledger","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to rebuild the Cartel's role in a fairer trade arrangement, and Veya and Maris want to see that the agreement lasts.","conflict":"Kael must accept the loss of his monopoly and the Cartel's pride, and the others must accept that old wounds will heal slowly.","outcome":"Kael opens a new ledger with shared tolls and wind-debts repaid fairly, and the three part as uneasy but real allies, each having learned the cost of acting alone.","summary":"Back at the docks, Kael starts a new ledger and the three part with a fragile peace, having woven the map, the grain and the ledger into one lasting plan.","depends_on":["scn_charts_shared"]}]}]}
