ile Kael is torn between exploiting the chaos and the disaster it could cause.","outcome":"Maris uses her service-corridor knowledge to bring the delegates to safety and Veya's wind-sight shows the spark came from tampered supplies; Kael is shaken but still hides his role.","summary":"A spark near the forge-pits nearly severs a bridge. The three work together to prevent disaster, and suspicion falls on Cartel supply lines."}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Accord","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_truth","title":"Truth on the Table","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share her complete charts with all three factions, and Kael wants to seize the last stable routes before the truce is signed.","conflict":"Sharing the charts means giving up her hoarded recognition and risks Cartel exploitation, while Kael's ledger-mastery lets him find the weak point in any arrangement, and Maris must defend the Hollow Circle's grain condition.","outcome":"Veya admits her mentor's theory was incomplete and shares the charts openly; Kael, facing the cost of control, concedes and the delegates agree to negotiate seriously.","summary":"At the Emberroost negotiating table, Veya lays out the whole map. Faced with the truth, Kael sees control costs more than it gains."},{"id":"scn_emberroost_accord_signed","title":"The Emberroost Accord","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"The three factions want to settle the toll, the grain levy, and the maintenance of the bridges in a single binding truce.","conflict":"Wind-debt obligations, the Cartel's tolls, and the Circle's demands threaten to collapse the talks at the final clause.","outcome":"The Accord is signed: tolls are capped and wind-debt can be repaid in cable-braiding labour, the grain levy is lifted, and the charts are held in common by the Wardens, Cartel, and Circle.","summary":"After tense bargai