{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Limits of Wind-sight","logline":"When Veya's wind-sight fails to foresee a new storm that shatters the skybridges, she must overcome her pride and share her charts with rivals and allies to keep the isles connected before the Drift Cartel seizes the last stable routes.","theme":"Truths shared are stronger than truths hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Blind Spot","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts","title":"Charts of a Fading Network","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to finish a chart of a safe route through the breaking skybridges, relying on her wind-sight to predict bridge movement.","conflict":"Her readings of the wind colours contradict the academy's older charts, and her stubbornness keeps her from asking colleagues to check her work.","outcome":"Veya completes a provisional route chart and, trusting her wind-sight, decides to keep it private until she can prove her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya uses wind-sight to chart a route through the failing skybridges, confident in her gift and unwilling to share unproven work.","depends_on":[]},{"id":"scn_docks_toll_offer","title":"A Charming Offer","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to confirm a bridge crossing at Mistral Docks, while Kael wants to acquire her new charts for the Cartel.","conflict":"Kael offers generous payment and protection for exclusive rights to the charts; Veya is tempted by recognition but refuses to let him control them, and the crossing accrues wind-debt she cannot easily repay.","outcome":"Veya turns Kael down. Kael, who admires her skill but cannot let her succeed, quietly resolves to make sure her charts never reach the other isles.","summary":"Kael, her former fellow apprentice, courts Veya at the docks for her charts. She refuses, and the rivalry hardens.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_charts"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_levy_secret","title":"The Quiet Silos","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a safe path for her survey and Maris wants to keep The Hollow fed despite the Cartel's grain levy.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya is a Cartel informant; Veya must prove herself without revealing how much her charts matter.","outcome":"Veya and Maris trade wind-current knowledge for Maris's service corridors, forming a cautious alliance that gives Veya an unmapped route.","summary":"On The Hollow, Veya earns Maris's wary trust by exchanging knowledge for access to secret corridors and silos.","depends_on":["scn_docks_toll_offer"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"The Storm Nobody Saw","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"Cables on the Anvil","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the Bridge Wardens at Emberroost to reinforce the bridges on her charted route; Kael wants to control the supply of braided cloudstone cable.","conflict":"The Wardens accuse Kael of sabotaging forge-island supplies, and the cable shortage means Veya's route cannot be reinforced in time.","outcome":"Veya gains evidence of the Cartel's interference but only a partial supply of cable, so her route stays fragile.","summary":"At the forge-island, Veya sees the Cartel's squeeze on cable supplies and confronts Kael over the sabotage claims.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_levy_secret"]},{"id":"scn_storm_unseen","title":"The Storm She Could Not Read","purpose_note":null,"location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to read the winds to warn The Hollow of incoming weather and protect the silos.","conflict":"A new storm forms with wind colours unlike any she has learned, and her wind-sight fails to predict it; her inability to admit error delays the warning.","outcome":"The storm severs a skybridge near The Hollow and damages the silos, and Maris is angered that Veya's confidence cost them time.","summary":"A storm Veya cannot foresee strikes. Her wind-sight reaches its limit and the damage strains her alliance with Maris."}]}]}

