ebuild her charts.","conflict":"Admitting she was wrong means exposing her private charts to scrutiny, and she fears becoming like the ambitious cartel leaders.","outcome":"Veya shares her charts and failure with the Academy cartographers, who combine them with survey records to model the storm's pattern and mark which bridges are still stable.","summary":"Humbled, Veya opens her work to the Academy. Shared survey knowledge, not wind-sight alone, begins to fill the gap.","depends_on":["scn_storm_unseen"]},{"id":"scn_docks_cartel_move","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the last stable skybridge routes; Maris wants to keep her smuggling routes open.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers close in on Maris's routes while Kael uses the storm panic to raise tolls and claim the stable bridges.","outcome":"Maris escapes with news of Kael's plan and the Cartel's claim, and is forced to choose between her isle and Veya.","summary":"As Kael tightens his grip on the stable routes, Maris is nearly caught and carries the warning back.","depends_on":["scn_storm_unseen"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Shared Map","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_alliance","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want the Wardens, Hollow Circle and Academy to adopt a shared route plan; Kael wants to stop it and keep control.","conflict":"Kael argues that only regulated trade can survive the collapse, while Maris's lingering distrust of Veya threatens the alliance.","outcome":"Veya publicly shares the full charts and admits her limits. Maris commits her corridors to the plan, and Kael's sabotage evidence undermines his standing.","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya confronts Kael with shared charts and Maris's corridors, and the isles choose cooperation over monopoly.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_admission","scn_docks_cartel_move","scn_emberroost_cables"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Storm","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_rebuild","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Rebuild the severed link to The Hollow and restore grain shipments.","conflict":"Cable is scarce, wind-debt is owed, and Maris still struggles to forgive Veya's earlier mistake.","outcome":"Wardens, millers and cartographers repay wind-debt in shared labour, the route is restored, and Maris and Veya renew their friendship.","summary":"The Hollow's windmills turn again as the shared route reopens.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_alliance"]},{"id":"scn_docks_kael_reckoning","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to salvage the Cartel's position; Veya wants a fair arrangement for tolls on the stable routes.","conflict":"Kael must weigh the cost of control against the benefit of cooperating after his sabotage has been exposed.","outcome":"Kael accepts reduced tolls under a shared charter, learning that control costs more than it gains, while Veya acknowledges that wind-sight alone could never have saved the isles.","summary":"At the docks, Kael and Veya settle a fragile peace, and the isles learn to survive by sharing knowledge.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_alliance","scn_hollow_rebuild"]}]}]}

