 would leave her isle short.","outcome":"She decides to smuggle grain through service corridors that appear on no chart.","summary":"Maris, who knows every hidden silo, watches the levy collectors arrive and starts planning to hide grain from them.","depends_on":["scn_kael_ledger_docks"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"Cables at Emberroost","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants the Bridge Wardens to confirm that the cloudstone cables are failing and to back her charts.","conflict":"The Wardens are short of supplies and wary of an academic who cannot prove her claims. Veya refuses to admit that her data has gaps.","outcome":"The Wardens grudgingly give her access to the cables and a warning that the Cartel is watching her.","summary":"At the forge-island, Veya inspects the braided cables and finds fraying that matches her predictions, but her stubbornness strains the Wardens' trust.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_survey"]}]},{"id":"act_two_toll_war","title":"The Toll War","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_offer","title":"Kael's Offer","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to acquire Veya's charts, and Veya wants to learn how much the Cartel knows.","conflict":"Their old rivalry and shared apprenticeship make them trust each other less. Kael admires her skill but cannot let her succeed, and she fears becoming ambitious like the cartel leaders.","outcome":"Veya refuses to hand over the charts. Kael responds by quietly ordering the Cartel to bury her work.","summary":"Kael charms and pressures Veya at the docks and offers her recognition in exchange for control of her charts. She leaves with her charts and a new enemy.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables"]},{"id":"scn_wind_debt_bargain","title":"A Debt of Wind","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to reach The Hollow, and Maris wants to learn whether Veya can be trusted.","conflict":"Every skybridge crossing accrues wind-debt that must be repaid within a season, and Veya is running short of goods. Maris trusts slowly and rarely forgives.","outcome":"They agree to trade wind-current knowledge for Maris's secret paths, and Veya pays the debt with a promise of labour.","summary":"Maris meets Veya at the busiest port and weighs her. They strike a bargain that makes them allies.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_levy_notice","scn_kael_offer"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_service_corridors","title":"Through the Service Corridors","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to move grain unseen, and Veya wants to map the unmarked corridors that bypass failing bridges.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers are closing in on the smuggling routes, and Maris is reluctant to reveal her secrets to an outsider.","outcome":"They slip past the enforcers, and Veya adds a safe route to her charts while Maris begins to trust her.","summary":"Maris leads Veya through windmills and granaries and they evade the enforcers, which strengthens their friendship.","depends_on":["scn_wind_debt_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_sabotage_claim","title":"Sabotage at Emberroost","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants proof that the Cartel has cut supplies to the forge-island, and Kael wants to deny it and discredit her.","conflict":"Cloudstone supplies are missing and the Wardens blame the Cartel. Kael presents ledgers that make the shortage look like the Wardens' mismanagement.","outcome":"Veya is shaken when her evidence proves inconclusive, and the Wardens withdraw some of their support.","summary":"A confrontation at the forge-pits exposes the Toll War. Kael outmaneuvers Veya, and her refusal to concede a mistake costs her allies.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offer","scn_hollow_service_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts_stolen","title":"The Charts Go Missing","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to present her findings to the academy and secure its support.","conflict":"Her working charts have been tampered with at the Cartel's instigation, and she cannot admit that she was careless in guarding them.","outcome":"She is left with only the route she memorised and the copy held by Maris, and she realises that hoarding her knowledge has made it vulnerable.","summary":"At the academy, Veya finds the charts destroyed or altered. Her pride and secrecy become liabilities.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_sabotage_claim"]}]},{"id":"act_three_breaking_point","title":"The Breaking Point","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_shares_truth","title":"Truth Shared","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to rebuild the charts openly and share them with every faction rather than hoard them.","conflict":"Admitting her earlier mistakes is painful for her, and Maris must decide whether to risk her home's secret corridors by adding them to a shared chart.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong and Maris contributes her paths. They produce a joint chart and spread copies to the Wardens and the Hollow Circle.","summary":"Veya breaks with her habit of secrecy and Maris chooses to stand openly beside her, so the new chart can no longer be buried.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_charts_stolen","scn_hollow_service_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_collapse_confrontation","title":"Confrontation on the Last Bridge","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to guide travellers across the failing network by her shared chart, and Kael wants to seize the last stable routes before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"Kael blocks the bridge with Cartel enforcers while the cables fray under strain. Only Veya's wind-sight and Maris's corridors offer a way through, and Kael must choose between control and the lives at stake.","outcome":"Kael sees that control costs more than it gains and stands aside. The Wardens, using the shared chart, redirect the crossing and the key bridge holds.","summary":"At the forge-island, the three characters meet at the failing bridge. The open chart defeats Kael's monopoly, and he yields.","depends_on":["scn_veya_shares_truth","scn_wardens_sabotage_claim"]}]},{"id":"act_four_new_currents","title":"New Currents","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_levy_lifted","title":"The Levy Lifted","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to settle the Cartel's position after the confrontation, and Maris wants the grain levy lifted for The Hollow.","conflict":"Cartel princes resist losing revenue, and Maris still distrusts Kael and will not forgive easily.","outcome":"Kael backs reduced tolls and an end to the levy, and Maris accepts the terms without forgiving him.","summary":"At the docks, Kael uses his ledger-mastery to renegotiate the Cartel's terms and ease the Toll War and the Grain Levy.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_collapse_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest_feast","title":"Harvest at The Hollow","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to see The Hollow fed and secure, and Veya wants to thank the people whose paths made the chart possible.","conflict":"Maris must weigh her long-held caution against her friendship with Veya, and Veya struggles with her need for recognition.","outcome":"Maris learns that sheltering can be as brave as standing in the open, and Veya credits her fully.","summary":"The windmills turn and the isle celebrates, and the two women reaffirm their alliance.","depends_on":["scn_docks_levy_lifted"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_new_atlas","title":"The Shared Atlas","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to establish an open atlas of the skybridge network that her late mentor's theory can inform.","conflict":"Kael's reconciliation with Veya is uneasy and the isles are still drifting, so the work will never be finished.","outcome":"The atlas is adopted by the Wardens, the Cartel and the Hollow Circle, and Veya, Kael and Maris each accept their new roles.","summary":"The three characters gather at the academy to open the atlas to all, and the story ends with the isles drifting but the people better prepared.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest_feast"]}]}]}
