{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Forgotten Wings","logline":"When the skybridges begin to fail, a stubborn cartographer who can only read the wind, not ride it, must chart a safe route on foot across the breaking network while a Drift Cartel toll-master tries to bury her charts and seize the last stable crossings.","theme":"Some truths are safer shared than hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Fraying Threads","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_discrepancy","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Confirm that her late mentor's theory is right by comparing her wind-sight readings with the Academy's archived bridge charts.","conflict":"The archived charts contradict her readings, and her stubborn pride makes her reluctant to share an unfinished finding with the Academy's Bridge Wardens.","outcome":"Veya concludes the isles are drifting apart and several skybridges will fail within a season, and she resolves to chart a safe route herself.","summary":"Alone in the Academy map vaults, Veya reads the colours of the wind currents against the old charts and finds the bridges are drifting out of alignment. She decides to keep the discovery private until she can prove it."},{"id":"scn_docks_toll_confrontation","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Cross a skybridge from the docks to reach the outer isles and test her predictions, without being stopped.","conflict":"Kael, her former fellow apprentice and now the Cartel's toll-master, demands a steep toll, adds to her wind-debt, and hints that he already suspects what her charts will show.","outcome":"Veya pays the toll and takes on a heavy wind-debt, and Kael makes it clear the Cartel wants any new charts buried.","summary":"At the busy docks, Kael charms and pressures Veya at the toll gate. She refuses to hand over her work, and the rivalry between them becomes open."},{"id":"scn_hollow_meeting_maris","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Find a way to reach the unstable bridge anchors on foot, since Veya has only wind-sight and cannot cross the gaps any other way.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya is working for the Cartel, while Veya has no safe corridors of her own and a wind-debt due.","outcome":"Veya and Maris agree to trade Veya's wind-current knowledge for Maris's unmapped service corridors.","summary":"Veya reaches the windmill isle and meets Maris. After a wary exchange, they strike an alliance: Veya shows her how to read the wind, and Maris offers her secret paths between the windmills and granaries."}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Breaking Bridges","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_cable_survey","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Inspect the cloudstone cables at the forge-island to measure how quickly the bridges are weakening.","conflict":"The Bridge Wardens are short of supplies and suspicious of outsiders, and no open flame is allowed outside the forge-pits, so the pair must work carefully by wind-sight and touch.","outcome":"They find evidence that cables are fraying faster than reported and that supplies have been diverted, which the Wardens blame on Kael.","summary":"At the forge-island, Veya reads the wind around the braided cables while Maris uses her corridors to move unseen. They learn the Wardens' supplies were deliberately cut off, and the Wardens recognise Veya's skill."},"id_placeholder_removed"]}]}

